ow she's not writing a marvel  movie but like you know she wrote uh  a book about the mindfulness of being a  jedi like she's doing really really cool  stuff and making a good living  doing  what she loves and talking about what  she loves so  i mean it is somebody you know if you're  like the only way that i will be happy  is if i'm writing a movie that a hundred  million people see  you know  at the risk of sounding like kevin like  adjust your expectations you know it's  your goal to be  a great actor or is your goal to be  famous if your goal is to make money  writing stories  that people will  see and enjoy and maybe you change  somebody from in that way  you don't need to  write a marvel television show to do  that you can write  you know a children's book that people  like me write read to their daughters  growing up that's going to change  the way that i relate to my daughter  because she loves the book and i love  star wars and and it's one of  three different star wars children's  books out there so i think part of it is  just looking at what's the actual goal  versus  what's the  dream goal you know what's the  what counts like what counts for being a  professional writer and if it's like i  want to  change people's lives with my words  that's a lot  different than being i want to be one of  the  600 people who gets a chance to  write star wars or marvel  you know  yeah  yeah you know if  it is as as jc said you know what is  what is the truth of it  um what do you want to be doing um  and writing as i said at the very job  takes lots of different forms what form  do you want to chase  um and there's parents  that all require a certain amount of  just dedication to it and resilience  there's going to be a lot more rejection  and there is acceptance and you have to  be okay with that um  and you have to do the work  because it's not going to come easy  um  and for those that it does come easy it  doesn't last  so  put in your reps  get uh get strong and ge